# Simple experimental RMK config for Saurus keyboard.

With Nix:
  nix develop
  cargo make uf2 --release

Install tools (when not using Nix):
  * Install the Arm GNU toolchain so `arm-none-eabi-gcc` and
    `arm-none-eabi-ar` are on PATH (for example, Debian/Ubuntu package
    `gcc-arm-none-eabi`).
  * Run `cargo install cargo-make flip-link`.

Then build with this command:
  cargo make uf2 --release

The firmware uses RMK 0.9 with Vial configuration available over USB. Rynk is
disabled because the two host protocols are mutually exclusive. Hold the
top-left and top-right keys to unlock Vial. `Cargo.toml` keeps both direct and
cargo-make builds on the RMK 0.9 release line.

XIAO nRF52840 battery/power support:
  * src/xiao.rs samples the 1M/510K divider on P0.31 with 40us SAADC
    acquisition and 16x hardware oversampling.
  * RMK drives P0.14 low before ADC setup and keeps it low for the firmware lifetime, as required by Seeed for safe battery sensing.
  * REG1 DC/DC is enabled; REG0 remains disabled because DCCH is not populated.
  * The unused onboard P25Q16H QSPI flash enters deep power-down at startup.

Hardware mapping was checked against the final reversible half-board in
../Saurus/pcb/Saurus.kicad_pcb and its 2025-09-25 Gerber export:
  * Rows 0..3 = P1.14, P1.13, P1.12, P1.11.
  * Cols 0..4 = P1.15, P0.29, P0.28, P0.03, P0.02.
  * The peripheral reverses those columns because the same PCB is mirrored.
  * Diode anodes face the columns and cathodes the rows, matching RMK col2row.
  * The thumb row occupies local columns 2..4, matching the layout map.
  * BAT+ connects directly to the XIAO BAT pad and BAT- to GND.
  * P0.14/P0.31 and P0.20..P0.25 are internal XIAO signals, not carrier nets.
The older pcb/production export describes a superseded 46-key/ProMicro design
and must not be used to validate this firmware.

After changing the low-level XIAO power code, flash one half first. Verify normal
boot, double-reset UF2 entry, INFO_UF2.TXT mounting, and UF2 reflashing before
updating the second half. The hardware-controlled charge LED is unchanged.
